A||||2||westtexas||4.9 bolt to 3.4 RWD transmission?||||1||
Z||000000||westtexas||09-22-2001||12:03 PM||||I started a Bubba Joe Caddy/Fiero swap this summer, bought mounts, rebuilt distributor, adapter plate from him, a 4.9 in good condition, and a '87 Fiero 2.5/auto with a bad engine. I wanted to do this swap so bad that I closed my mind to the facts: A carbed engine swapped in an originally fuel injected car won't pass inspection in Texas. Still being drunk in my Fiero addition, I bought a new 4.9 long block from Ed Parks recently and plan to use his swap kit instead when it finally comes out (didn't know he was making a kit when I started Bubba Joe's version). I'm thinking of swapping my carbed 4.9 in a '83 Nissan pickup that came with a carb and using a RWD transmission from a 3.4 V6 '93 to '95 Camero. I'm assuming the Cad will bolt to the Camero trans bellhousing. What about the flywheel and clutch? Thanks for any help. <P>Live for Fieros, work to support addiction,<BR>Robert||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||09-22-2001||03:26 PM||||The engine should bolt to the trans without any trouble, the basic pattern is the same. You may need to do some clearancing for the starter. A re-drilled Camaro flywheel should work fine or you can get a new custom one made. <P>Why not use the Cadillac fuel injection and put the engine in the Fiero? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||westtexas||09-22-2001||10:26 PM||||<BR>Why not use the Cadillac fuel injection and put the engine in the Fiero? [/B][/QUOTE]<P>Rockcrawl, I sent my Cad distributor to Bubba Joe and he put Olds HEI internals and a faster advance curve in it. So, to be legal and use Bubba Joe's method, I need to buy another stock distributor, '89 computer, harness, and throttle body. Now, Ed Parks may have a harness/computer that will work with the sequential fuel injection soon but I believe his also will use the Cad transmission. I'm a few moons past the half century mark and most of my experience is with simpler engines. I was planning on doing a simple swap. I could just bolt it together with  very quite mufflers and act dumb. "You mean that's not stock?" Maybe if I tried enough inspection stations one would pass it. <P>Applying the Peter Principle (rising to my level of incompetance for the less than 25 yr olds),<BR>Robert<P>||||reg||1
